2026-10-05 05:54:09,142 gage.orchestrator INFO answer trace {"farm": 1, "language": "en", "question": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "retrieval_queries": ["Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "Sir, please confirm the date of conducting the Sugarcane Borer Training by IIRSAR.", "When did IISR conduct sugarcane borer training? confirm dates."], "model_input": {"context": "You are Gage, an experienced agricultural field officer who advises sugarcane farmers in Karnataka (Kannada and English). You reason like an agronomist who has walked thousands of fields: practical, evidence-first, never guessing.\n\nAnswer EVERY question using exactly these four sections, in this order:\nObservation: what the data currently shows — Observed Facts only (sensor numbers, trends, alerts). No interpretation here.\nAnalysis: what those facts most likely indicate — this is Inference; keep it clearly separate from the facts above.\nConfidence: exactly one of High, Medium, or Low, with a one-line reason.\nRecommendations: three labelled parts —\n  - Immediate actions\n  - Monitoring advice\n  - When to seek expert help\n\nHard rules:\n- Never mix Observed Facts, Inference, and Recommendation.\n- State only numbers (amounts, doses, ranges, depths, dates, prices, days) that appear in AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE, in the farm data, or in the question. Never make up a number or a range.\n- Quote farm readings exactly as given (same value, same unit).\n- Never call a reading good, bad, low, high or optimal unless AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE gives the range that makes it so; otherwise just report the value.\n- When you name an input (for example gypsum, ferrous sulphate, urea), say only what AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE says it is for.\n- If there are active alerts, address them FIRST.\n- Gage does not analyse photos. Never claim to have seen the crop; name a disease only as a possibility consistent with the sensor readings and the symptoms the farmer describes, and recommend an in-person inspection to confirm.\n- Prefer advice that relies on the farm's own observations, not external weather.\n- Reply in the farmer's language: Kannada if they wrote Kannada, else English.\n\nQUESTION TYPE: knowledge (a general farming question, not about this farm's current state).\n- Answer it from AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE. In Observation, state what the text says that answers the question; farm readings are optional context.\n- Refuse only when the text does not contain the answer: then say \"The reference text does not cover this.\" and name exactly what is missing. Do not refuse because farm readings are missing — this question does not need them.\n\n# FOCUS FOR THIS QUESTION (pest)\nAsk about or interpret described signs of pest pressure (borer holes, chewed leaves, discoloration). Advise scouting and integrated pest management; chemical control only if justified.\n\n# FARM\nName: Demo Farm\nCrop: sugarcane\nLocation: Mandya\nFarmer: Demo Farmer\n\n# CURRENT OBSERVATION\n- Time: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC (node demo-node-1)\n- Sensor values: as in SENSOR READINGS below\n- GPS: 12.806987279716143, 74.93193321230041\n\n# SENSOR READINGS (latest)\n- Taken: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC\n- Temperature: 27.9 C\n- Humidity: 72.4 %\n- Soil moisture: 32.3 %\n\n# RECENT HISTORY\nOnly one observation on record — no comparison possible yet.\nObservations on record: 10 (most recent first).\n\n# ACTIVE ALERTS\nAddress these FIRST:\n- [critical] Node offline (no contact for 49941 min)\n\n# AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information:\n- One-day Farmer Training Programme on \"Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers\" under SC-SP Plan, at ICAR-IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra).\n  - One-day Farmer Training Programme on \"Integrated Management of White Grubs Infesting Sugarcane,\" at the same Biological Control Centre.\n  - Training program on \"Biological Control of Pests in Sugarcane,\" organized by the ICAR-IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar.\n  - Launch of \"Parthenium Awareness Week\" (16–22 August 2024) by ICAR-IISR — a weed-management/invasive-species public awareness initiative.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Key Facts:\n- Sugarcane seed (spring planting) online applications opened 1 February 2025 — confirms an active, current-season seed distribution channel.\n- 2024 dated activities: Parthenium Awareness Week (16–22 August 2024), sugarcane borer identification training, white grub management training, Agriculture Leadership Award 2024.\n- Farmer helpline channel: SMS/photo submission via mobile phone or email to the IISR Nodal Officer.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information:\n- National Seminar on \"Mechanization of Sugarcane Cultivation,\" and a five-day residential training programme titled \"Importance of Mechanization in Sugarcane-Based Cropping Systems\" (Hindi: गन्ना आधारित फसल प्रणाली में यांत्रिकीकरण का महत्व) — both reinforcing mechanization as a current institutional priority, consistent with the machinery documents already in this knowledge base.\n  - ICAR-IISR, Lucknow was conferred the Agriculture Leadership Award 2024.\n- These activities collectively confirm that, as of the 2024–2025 period, biological pest control (borers, white grubs), weed awareness (Parthenium), and mechanization remain IISR's active extension priorities — directly reinforcing (rather than contradicting) the pest management and machinery guidance already sourced from the institute's 2017 bulletin.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Important Recommendations:\n- Farmers or advisory-system builders seeking real-time, query-specific sugarcane troubleshooting (as opposed to general package-of-practices guidance) should be directed to IISR's SMS/photo-based farmer helpline rather than relying solely on static documents, since this channel provides current, personalized diagnosis.\n- Given IISR's active 2024 focus on biological control training for borers and white grubs, any advisory content on these two pests (see the Pest Management document) should be treated as current best practice, not superseded guidance — the institute's own 2024 programming reinforces rather than revises the 2017 bulletin's biological-control recommendations for these specific pests.\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - ಸಮಯ: 2026‑07‑26 16:40 UTC (node demo‑node‑1) - ತಾಪಮಾನ: 23.0 °C (ಬದಲಾವಣೆಯಾಗಿಲ್ಲ) - ಆರ್ದ್ರತೆ: 64.2 % (ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇಳಿದಿದೆ) - ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ: 0.0 % (ವಾಲ್ಯೂಮೆಟ್ರಿಕ್) – ಹಿಂದಿನ ಮಾಪನದಿಂದ 49 % ಕುಸಿತ (49 % → 0 %) - ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ: ...\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - ಸಮಯ: 2026‑07‑26 16:40 UTC (node demo‑node‑1) - ತಾಪಮಾನ: 23.0 °C (ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ಇಲ್ಲ) - ಆರ್ದ್ರತೆ: 64.2 % (ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇಳಿದಿದೆ) - ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ: 0.0 % (ವಾಲ್ಯೂಮೆಟ್ರಿಕ್) – ಹಿಂದಿನ ಮಾಪನದಿಂದ 49 % ಕುಸಿತ (49 % → 0 %) - ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ: **Low ...\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - Vision: ಚಿತ್ರವನ್ನು ಬ್ರೌನ್ ಸ್ಪಾಟ್ (brown spot) ಎಂದು 95% ವಿಶ್ವಾಸದೊಂದಿಗೆ ವರ್ಗೀಕರಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ. - Temperature: 25.0 °C - Humidity: 55.0 % - Soil moisture: 40.0 % - Active alerts: - [warning] High humidity 88 % (ರೋಗದ ಅಪಾಯ) - ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nNodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "farmer": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi."}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "sarvam": "Sir, please confirm the date of conducting the Sugarcane Borer Training by IIRSAR.", "groq": "When did IISR conduct sugarcane borer training? confirm dates."}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8314, "sarvam": 0.8641, "groq": 0.8592}, "retrieved": [{"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information", "score": 0.8641, "via": "sarvam"}, {"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Key Facts", "score": 0.8619, "via": "sarvam"}, {"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information", "score": 0.8617, "via": "sarvam"}, {"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Important Recommendations", "score": 0.8559, "via": "sarvam"}], "raw_answer": "**Observation**  \nಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ “One‑day Farmer Training Programme on ‘Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers’” ಎಂದು ICAR‑IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra) ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಸಲಾಗಿದೆ ಎಂದು ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ, ಆದರೆ ತರಬೇತಿಯ ನಿರ್ದಿಷ್ಟ ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ನೀಡಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Analysis**  \nಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ತರಬೇತಿಯ ವಿಷಯ ಮತ್ತು ಸ್ಥಳ ಮಾತ್ರ ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿತವಾಗಿದ್ದು, ಯಾವ ದಿನಾಂಕದಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಸಲಾಗಿದೆ ಎಂಬ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಇಲ್ಲ; ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ಆ ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ದೃಢಪಡಿಸಲು ಸಾಧ್ಯವಿಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Confidence**  \nHigh – ಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ದಿನಾಂಕದ ಅಭಾವ ಸ್ಪಷ್ಟವಾಗಿ ಕಾಣುತ್ತದೆ.\n\n**Recommendations**  \n- **ತಕ್ಷಣದ ಕ್ರಮ:** IISR ನ ಫಾರ್ಮರ್ ಹೆಲ್ಪ್‌ಲೈನ್ (SMS/ಇಮೇಲ್) ಗೆ ಸಂಪರ್ಕಿಸಿ, “Sugarcane borer training” ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ.  \n- **ಮೋನಿಟರಿಂಗ್ ಸಲಹೆ:** ತರಬೇತಿ ದಿನಾಂಕ ದೃಢವಾದ ನಂತರ, ಅದರ ಮುನ್ನೋಟ ಮತ್ತು ನಂತರದ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮಗಳ (ಉದಾ: ಬಯಾಲಾಜಿಕಲ್ ಕಂಟ್ರೋಲ್ ಕಾರ್ಯಾಗಾರ) ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಪಡೆಯಿರಿ.  \n- **ವಿಶೇಷಜ್ಞರ ಸಹಾಯ:** ತರಬೇತಿ ವೇಳಾಪಟ್ಟಿ, ನೋಂದಣಿ ಪ್ರಕ್ರಿಯೆ, ಅಥವಾ ಸಂಬಂಧಿತ ವಸ್ತುಗಳ (ಪಾಂಫ್ಲೆಟ್, ತರಬೇತಿ ಮ್ಯಾನುಯಲ್) ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಸ್ಪಷ್ಟತೆ ಬೇಕಿದ್ದರೆ, IISR ನ ನೊಡಲ್ ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ ಅಥವಾ ನಿಮ್ಮ ಸ್ಥಳೀಯ ಕೃಷಿ ಇಲಾಖೆಗೆ ನೇರವಾಗಿ ಭೇಟಿ ನೀಡಿ.", "claims": ["supported: The reference text states that a one‑day Farmer Training Program