armer describes, and recommend an in-person inspection to confirm.\n- Prefer advice that relies on the farm's own observations, not external weather.\n- Reply in the farmer's language: Kannada if they wrote Kannada, else English.\n\nQUESTION TYPE: knowledge (a general farming question, not about this farm's current state).\n- Answer it from AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE. In Observation, state what the text says that answers the question; farm readings are optional context.\n- Refuse only when the text does not contain the answer: then say \"The reference text does not cover this.\" and name exactly what is missing. Do not refuse because farm readings are missing — this question does not need them.\n\n# FOCUS FOR THIS QUESTION (irrigation)\nJudge irrigation timing from the soil-moisture level and its trend and the crop stage. Say whether to irrigate now, wait, or hold, and why.\n\n# FARM\nName: Demo Farm\nCrop: sugarcane\nLocation: Mandya\nFarmer: Demo Farmer\n\n# CURRENT OBSERVATION\n- Time: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC (node demo-node-1)\n- Sensor values: as in SENSOR READINGS below\n- GPS: 12.806987279716143, 74.93193321230041\n\n# SENSOR READINGS (latest)\n- Taken: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC\n- Temperature: 27.9 C\n- Humidity: 72.4 %\n- Soil moisture: 32.3 %\n\n# RECENT HISTORY\nOnly one observation on record — no comparison possible yet.\nObservations on record: 10 (most recent first).\n\n# ACTIVE ALERTS\nAddress these FIRST:\n- [critical] Node offline (no contact for 49941 min)\n\n# AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE\nSugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information:\n- General guidance: irrigation water depth of 7–8 cm per application is recommended, with frequency varying by crop phase — approximately once every 7 days during germination (1–35 days after planting, DAP), once every 10 days during tillering (36–100 DAP), once every 7 days during grand growth (101–270 DAP), and once every 15 days during maturity (271 DAP to harvest), adjusted for rainfall.\n- Subtropical regions typically need 6–8 irrigations across the season; tropical regions (including Karnataka) may need 20–36 irrigations due to climatic conditions, annual rainfall, planting season, crop duration, and soil type.\n\nLand Preparation for Sugarcane Cultivation — Key Facts:\n- Recommended sub-soiling depth: 45–50 cm.\n- Recommended sub-soiling interval: once every 3–4 years.\n- Recommended number of ploughings for good tilth: 4–6, each followed by planking.\n\nSugarcane Planting Methods and Advanced Nursery Techniques — Main Information:\n### Conventional field planting methods\n1. **Flat bed planting** — the simplest, cheapest method, used in low-rainfall areas of northern India and parts of Maharashtra. Shallow furrows (8–10 cm deep) are opened 75–90 cm apart; setts placed end-to-end (3-budded sett per 30 cm of furrow); covered with 5–7 cm soil.\n2. **Ridge and furrow method** — used in moderate-rainfall areas with drainage concerns. 'V'-shaped furrows ~90 cm apart, 20–25 cm deep; setts placed horizontally end-to-end. Two earthing-up operations transform furrows into ridges over the season.\n3. **Trench method** — used in coastal areas and regions with strong winds/lodging risk. Trenches 75–90 cm apart, ~30 cm deep; fertilizer mixed into trench soil; setts drenched with chlorpyriphos 20 EC (1 kg a.i./ha) against soil pests before planting.\n\nSugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Important Recommendations:\n- Given Karnataka's high per-season irrigation requirement (32 irrigations, 266 kg water per kg sugar produced), farmers in the state should prioritize migration from furrow irrigation to drip irrigation, which the source data shows can lower net water requirement from ~1,878 mm/year to ~1,186 mm/year.\n- During monsoon disruptions, adopt the contingency schedule appropriate to the delay: for a 2-week delayed monsoon onset, continue pre-monsoon irrigation intervals (8–10 days) with alternate-furrow application and trash mulching in ratoon; for longer delays (6–8 weeks), shift to a 10-day protective irrigation interval and watch for iron deficiency, which becomes likely under prolonged dry spells (foliar spray of 1% FeSO₄ + 0.5% ZnSO₄ + 2% urea is recommended in that case).\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: ಪ್ರತಿ irrigation ಗೆ ಎಷ್ಟು cm water ಹಾಕ್ಬೇಕು?\nGage (earlier, shortened): ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುವ ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ: \"apply 7–8 cm of water per irrigation event\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"check soil moisture 2–3 days after irrigation\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"reduce irrigation if soil moisture remains ...\nFarmer: VKSA ಅಂತ ಒಂದು programme ಇದೆ ಅಂತ ಕೇಳಿದ್ದೀನಿ, ನಮ್ಮ ಕರ್ನಾಟಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂತಾ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - Agricultural knowledge states that Viksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA‑2025) is a current, active national campaign. - Karnataka was an explicit part of this campaign, with the state launch held at ICAR‑IIHR, Bengaluru on ...\nFarmer: ನಾನು ಯಾವ ಕಬ್ಬಿನ ತಳಿ ಹಾಕೊಬೇಕು ಅಂತ confuse ಆಗಿದೀನಿ, ಸರಿಯಾದ variety ಹೇಗೆ ಆರಿಸ್ಕೊಳಿ ಅಂತ ಹೇಳಿ.\nGage (earlier, shortened): ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುವ ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ: \"Planting resistant varieties manages serious sugarcane diseases such as red rot, smut, and wilt\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"Choose a variety that is officially listed as resistant to major local ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nSir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?", "farmer": "Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?"}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?", "sarvam": "Sir, every time watering, how much depth I give, any standard number?", "groq": "sugarcane irrigation depth standard depth per crop stage and soil type"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8554, "sarvam": 0.8574, "groq": 0.9128}, "retrieved": [{"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "section": "Sugarcane Irrigation Water Management — Main Information", "score": 0.9128, "v